<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.Rot2Fwd(Rotation: rotation): vector`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`vector llRot2Fwd(rotation Rotation);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p class="deprecated-text"><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>Deprecated:  use quaternion.tofwd</span></p>
      <p>  <p>Computes the orientation of the local x-axis relative to the parent (i.e. the root prim or the world).</p>
  <p>Returns a vector that is the forward vector defined by <b>q</b>, i.e. a unit vector pointing in the local positive X direction.</p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>rotation</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>rotation</span></td>
          <td>Rotation / q</td>
          <td></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>math</li>
        <li>math_3d</li>
        <li>math_trig</li>
        <li>quaternion</li>
        <li>vector</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">18</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
        <span class="attr-label bg-pure">Side-Effect Free</span>
        <span class="lua-section attr-label bg-deprecated">Lua Deprecated</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <h2>Specification</h2>
  <p>Mathematically equivalent to:</p>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`ret = llVecNorm(<1., 0., 0.> * q);`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>If <b>q</b> is known to be a unit quaternion then it can be simplified as:</p>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`ret = <1., 0., 0.> * q;`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>Keep in mind that object and agent rotations will always be unit quaternions. For example, <1.0, 0.0, 0.0>*llGetRot() is about 25-30% faster than llRot2Fwd(llGetRot()) depending on the VM used. If done often and at extremely fast rates, it can be advantageous to even save <1.0, 0.0, 0.0> to a local/global variable and reuse it.</p>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`-- Move an object 5 metres forwards along its x axis, when touched, no matter how the object is oriented in world.
-- Works for a root or child prim
function LLEvents.touch_start(events)
    local total_number = #events
    local v = ll.Rot2Fwd(ll.GetLocalRot())
    ll.SetPos(ll.GetLocalPos() + v * 5)
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`// Move an object 5 metres forwards along its x axis, when touched, no matter how the object is oriented in world.
// Works for a root or child prim
default
{
    touch_start(integer total_number)
    {
        vector v = llRot2Fwd( llGetLocalRot() );
        llSetPos( llGetLocalPos() + v * 5 );
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <p>Can be useful to identify the orientation of the local frontal-plane of the prim, since its x-axis is always perpendicular to this local frontal plane.</p>
